13	 * the request or defaulted to the server date) is a Saturday or Sunday, or a listed public holiday,
14	 * it is rolled forward to the next non-holiday weekday; an ordinary weekday is left unchanged.
15	 */
16	public final class BusinessDays {
17	
18	    /** Fixed public holidays the business-day roll skips. */
19	    static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
20	            LocalDate.parse("2026-01-01"), LocalDate.parse("2026-01-26"),
21	            LocalDate.parse("2026-04-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-25"),
22	            LocalDate.parse("2026-12-28"));
23	
24	    private BusinessDays() {
25	    }
26	
27	    /**
28	     * The registration date an owner will actually be stored with: the supplied date, or the
29	     * server's current date when none was supplied, rolled off a weekend onto a business day.
30	     * Single source of truth shared by every step that needs the effective date, so they cannot
31	     * drift apart.
32	     */
33	    public static LocalDate effectiveRegistrationDate(LocalDate supplied) {
34	        return toBusinessDay(supplied != null ? supplied : LocalDate.now());
35	    }
36	
37	    /**
38	     * The number of owners already registered on the given business day. Single source of truth for
39	     * the per-day signup count, shared by the daily-limit and bulk-signup rules so their counts
40	     * cannot drift apart; each rule keeps only its own threshold and action. Counts persisted owners
41	     * only, so a step calling this before {@code SaveOwner} does not count the owner being created.
42	     */
43	    public static long createdOn(OwnerRepository ownerRepository, LocalDate businessDay) {
44	        return ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
45	                .filter(existing -> businessDay.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))
46	                .count();
47	    }
48	
49	    /**
50	     * Roll a date forward over weekends and listed public holidays to the next business day;
51	     * an ordinary weekday that is not a holiday is returned unchanged.
52	     */
53	    public static LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate date) {
54	        LocalDate adjusted = date;
55	        while (adjusted.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY
56	                || adjusted.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY
57	                || HOLIDAYS.contains(adjusted)) {
58	            adjusted = adjusted.plusDays(1);
59	        }
60	        return adjusted;
61	    }
62	}
