13	 *
14	 * <p>The code is formatted {@code <REGION>-<HASH8>}:
15	 * <ul>
16	 * <li>{@code REGION} is the owner's region code, derived from the postcode (see
17	 * {@link OwnerRegion#localityOf}, which prefers the postcode and falls back to the city table), e.g.
18	 * {@code NSW}.</li>
19	 * <li>{@code HASH8} is the first eight upper-case hex characters of the SHA-256 of
20	 * {@code normalizedTelephone + lastName}, where {@code normalizedTelephone} is the E.164 telephone
21	 * (see {@link OwnerTelephone#toE164}).</li>
22	 * </ul>
23	 *
24	 * <p>There are no sequence numbers: the code depends only on the owner's own region, telephone and
25	 * last name, so it can be computed without coordinating through the database. Every other identity
26	 * value is derived from this code — the membership number and its Luhn check digit, the create audit
27	 * record and the read-time {@code locality} all read the region-and-hash code assigned here.
28	 */
29	public final class OwnerCustomerCode {
